% Chapter 91 of the tariff (Section XVIII): clocks and watches and parts
% thereof — all fourteen headings (9101 to 9114) and their 48 six-digit
% subheadings. A library: it includes chapter_42.le (and through it
% chapter_64.le, chapter_71.le, chapter_39.le, section_xi.le and gri.le),
% because the notes of Chapters 39, 42 and 71 send the articles of this
% chapter out of those chapters, and because this chapter reads the metals
% of Chapter 71; tariff.le includes it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 23 (2026), Chapter 91 notes 1 to 4, Additional U.S.
% notes 1 to 3, and the terms of the headings and subheadings
% (https://hts.usitc.gov/). Chapter 91 has no subheading notes. The
% subheadings are the six-digit HS ones. US Customs rulings say how the
% notes are read: a case with a steel bezel or a steel back is not wholly of
% precious metal (HQ 968150); a bracelet of steel inlaid with gold is of
% metal clad with precious metal (HQ 965207); watch straps of any material
% are of heading 9113 (HQ 951467, HQ H276954); a smart watch is no watch of
% heading 9102 (HQ H260060).
%
% How the chapter is read. The facts of a good are what it is (its kind: a
% wrist watch, an alarm clock, a watch movement, a watch strap, a dial...),
% and the features the headings and subheadings name:
%   G is electrically operated               (a quartz or a digital watch)
%   G has a mechanical movement               (driven by a spring)
%   G has automatic winding
%   G has a mechanical display / an opto-electronic display
%   G incorporates a stand                    (Additional U.S. note 1(a))
%   G has a watch movement                    (a clock, heading 9103)
%   G measures N mm in thickness / in width   (a movement, note 3)
%   G is for a watch                          (a movement set, heading 9110)
%   the case metal of W is M; the case of W is clad with M; the case of W
%       has a part of M                       (a watch, note 2)
% and for straps and cases the metal of Chapter 71 ("the metal of G is
% stainless steel", "G is clad with gold"), "G is inlaid with gold", "G is
% made of plastics" (Chapter 39), "G is wholly or mainly of leather".
% The chapter then decides:
%   WATCHES (9101, 9102): a timepiece for wearing or carrying on the person
%   (Additional U.S. note 1(a)) with a case wholly of precious metal or of
%   metal clad with precious metal is of 9101 (note 2); every other watch is
%   of 9102. The subheadings read the form (wrist watch or other), the power
%   (electrically operated or not), the display and automatic winding.
%   CLOCKS (9103 to 9105): a clock with a watch movement is of 9103; a clock
%   for a vehicle is of 9104; every other clock is of 9105, by its group
%   (alarm clock, wall clock, other) and its power.
%   APPARATUS (9106, 9107): time recorders, parking meters, time switches.
%   MOVEMENTS (9108 to 9110): a watch movement (note 3: not over 12 mm thick
%   and not over 50 mm wide), a clock movement (Additional U.S. note 1(d)),
%   movement sets, incomplete and rough movements.
%   CASES, STRAPS, PARTS (9111 to 9114): watch cases by their material,
%   clock cases, watch straps by their material (precious metal, base metal,
%   other), dials, plates and bridges, and the other parts.
% Note 1 takes some goods out of the chapter: clock or watch glasses and
% weights, watch chains, bearing balls, ball bearings; Additional U.S. note 3
% takes batteries entered alone. Chapter 39 note 2(v) and Chapter 71 note
% 3(l) send the articles of this chapter out of those chapters; Chapter 42
% note 4 takes watch straps out of heading 4203 (all written below).
% A smart watch is no watch of heading 9102 (HQ H260060): it is no article of
% this chapter, and the claim that it belongs to heading 8517 is answered by
% the office (gri.le).
%
% Not modelled: the lines below six digits (jewels, values, the material of
% the strap of a watch); note 1(c) (parts of general use: section XV), 1(e)
% and 1(g) (articles of chapters 84 and 85); note 4. A watch whose display
% or power the facts do not state gets its heading but no subheading.
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a family* is a family of chapter ninety-one goods.
    *a family* is the family of heading *a heading*.
    *a kind* is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover.
    *a good* is an article of chapter ninety-one.
    *a kind* is a kind of wrist watch.
    *a kind* is a kind of alarm clock.
    *a kind* is a kind of wall clock.
    *a kind* is a kind of case part.
    *a kind* is a kind of movement plate.
    *a good* differs substantially from the watches of heading 9102.
    *a good* is a watch.
    *a good* is a clock.
    *a good* incorporates a stand; undefined.
    *a good* is electrically operated; undefined.
    *a good* has a mechanical movement; undefined.
    *a good* has automatic winding; undefined.
    *a good* has a mechanical display; undefined.
    *a good* has an opto-electronic display; undefined.
    *a good* has a watch movement; undefined.
    *a good* measures *a number* mm in thickness; undefined.
    *a good* measures *a number* mm in width; undefined.
    *a good* is for a watch; undefined.
    *a good* is of watch size.
    *a good* is of clock size.
    *a good* is a watch movement.
    *a good* is a clock movement.
    the case metal of *a watch* is *a metal*; undefined.
    the case of *a watch* is clad with *a metal*; undefined.
    the case of *a watch* has a part of *a metal*; undefined.
    *a watch* has a case of precious metal.
    *a thing* is inlaid with *a metal*; undefined.
    *a good* is entered with *a watch*; undefined.
    *a thing* is of a material other than metal.
    the material class of *a thing* is *a class*.
    the timepiece form of *a good* is *a form*.
    the power class of *a good* is *a power*.
    the display class of *a good* is *a display*.
    the winding class of *a good* is *a winding*.
    the part class of *a good* in heading *a heading* is *a class*.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for the form *a form* with power *a power* with display *a display* with winding *a winding* is *a code* under table timepieces.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for the part class *a class* is *a code* under table timepiece parts.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6 for the watches, the clocks and the movements (9101 to 9105, 9108,
% 9109). First match: an "any" row is the series' "Other". The form is that
% of a watch (wrist watch, other watch), of a clock (alarm, wall, other) or
% "movement"; the power is electric or mechanical; the display is
% mechanical, opto-electronic, combined (both) or unstated; the winding is
% automatic or none. An electrically operated wrist watch or movement whose
% display is unstated matches no row: its subheading is left open.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% the six-digit subheadings of the timepieces
the table timepieces is, with first match, with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
    row | heading | form        | power      | display                       | winding   | code      | as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91
    t1  | 9101    | wrist       | electric   | mechanical                    | any       | "9101.11" | "With mechanical display only: 9101.11"
    t2  | 9101    | wrist       | electric   | opto-electronic or combined   | any       | "9101.19" | "Other: 9101.19"
