% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the goods of the chapter's families.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the clocks, the watches and their parts
rule timepiece_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter ninety-one goods.

watch is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches".
clock is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks".
vehicle clock is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Instrument panel clocks and clocks of a similar type for vehicles, aircraft, spacecraft or vessels".
time apparatus is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time of day recording apparatus and apparatus for measuring, recording or otherwise indicating intervals of time".
time switch is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time switches with clock or watch movement or with synchronous motor".
movement is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch movements, complete and assembled".
movement set is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Complete watch or clock movements, unassembled or partly assembled (movement sets)".
watch case is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch cases and parts thereof".
clock case is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock cases and cases of a similar type for other goods of this chapter, and parts thereof".
watch strap is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof".
watch part is a family of chapter ninety-one goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clock or watch parts".

% the families that a heading names alone
vehicle clock is the family of heading 9104,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Instrument panel clocks and clocks of a similar type for vehicles, aircraft, spacecraft or vessels".
time apparatus is the family of heading 9106,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time of day recording apparatus and apparatus for measuring, recording or otherwise indicating intervals of time".
time switch is the family of heading 9107,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time switches with clock or watch movement or with synchronous motor".
movement set is the family of heading 9110,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Complete watch or clock movements, unassembled or partly assembled (movement sets); incomplete watch or clock movements, assembled; rough watch or clock movements".
watch case is the family of heading 9111,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch cases and parts thereof".
clock case is the family of heading 9112,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock cases and cases of a similar type for other goods of this chapter, and parts thereof".
watch strap is the family of heading 9113,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof".
watch part is the family of heading 9114,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clock or watch parts".

% The kinds of the chapter's goods and their families: the tariff's own
% words, and the words of the rulings
wrist watch falls in the family watch, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches".
pocket watch falls in the family watch, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches".
stop watch falls in the family watch, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches".
watch head falls in the family watch, as stated in ruling HQ 968150, confer "“Watch head” is the industry term given to a watch sold without a strap, band, or bracelet".
pendant watch falls in the family watch, as stated in ruling NY N233953, confer "The necklace watch is a gold-plated pendent watch".
smart watch falls in the family watch, as stated in ruling HQ H260060, confer "wearable electronic device in the form of a wrist-watch".
wrist watch is a kind of wrist watch, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wrist watches, electrically operated, whether or not incorporating a stop watch facility".
smart watch is a kind of wrist watch, as stated in ruling HQ H260060, confer "wearable electronic device in the form of a wrist-watch".

clock falls in the family clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks".
alarm clock falls in the family clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Alarm clocks".
wall clock falls in the family clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wall clocks".
desk clock falls in the family clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks".
table clock falls in the family clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks".
alarm clock is a kind of alarm clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Alarm clocks".
wall clock is a kind of wall clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wall clocks".
instrument panel clock falls in the family vehicle clock, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Instrument panel clocks and clocks of a similar type for vehicles".
time recorder falls in the family time apparatus, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time registers; time-recorders".
time register falls in the family time apparatus, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time registers; time-recorders".
parking meter falls in the family time apparatus, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Parking meters".
time switch falls in the family time switch, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time switches with clock or watch movement or with synchronous motor".

watch movement falls in the family movement, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch movements, complete and assembled".
clock movement falls in the family movement, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock movements, complete and assembled".
movement falls in the family movement, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "the expression \"watch movements\" means devices regulated by a balance wheel and hairspring".
movement set falls in the family movement set, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Complete movements, unassembled or partly assembled (movement sets)".
incomplete movement falls in the family movement set, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Incomplete movements, assembled".
rough movement falls in the family movement set, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Rough movements".

watch case falls in the family watch case, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch cases and parts thereof".
case back falls in the family watch case, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "The term \"cases\" embraces inner and outer cases, containers and housings for movements, together with parts or pieces".
case part falls in the family watch case, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "The term \"cases\" embraces inner and outer cases, containers and housings for movements, together with parts or pieces".
bezel falls in the family watch case, as stated in ruling HQ 968150, confer "Accordingly, the bezels are embraced in the definition of “cases” set forth in Additional U.S. Note 1(b)".
spring bar falls in the family watch case, as stated in ruling HQ 951467, confer "the spring-bars are classifiable under 9111.90.70, HTSUS".
case back is a kind of case part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "such as, but not limited to, rings, feet, posts, bases and outer frames".
case part is a kind of case part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "together with parts or pieces".
bezel is a kind of case part, as stated in ruling HQ 968150, confer "the bezels on the watches at issue are parts that “serve to complete” the watches at issue".
spring bar is a kind of case part, as stated in ruling HQ 951467, confer "the spring-bars are classifiable under 9111.90.70, HTSUS".
clock case falls in the family clock case, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock cases and cases of a similar type".
clock case part falls in the family clock case, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock cases and cases of a similar type for other goods of this chapter, and parts thereof".
clock case part is a kind of case part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock cases and cases of a similar type for other goods of this chapter, and parts thereof".

watch strap falls in the family watch strap, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof".
watch band falls in the family watch strap, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof".
watch bracelet falls in the family watch strap, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof".
watch strap part falls in the family watch strap, as stated in ruling NY 884636, confer "is an unfinished part of a watch bracelet known in the trade as a \"stick.\"".

dial falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Dials".
watch hand falls in the family watch part, as stated in ruling NY N170879, confer "The applicable subheading for the watch hands and stems will be 9114.90.40".
stem falls in the family watch part, as stated in ruling NY N170879, confer "The applicable subheading for the watch hands and stems will be 9114.90.40".
crown falls in the family watch part, as stated in the Wikipedia article Watch, confer "a small knob, called the crown, that can be used to adjust the time and, in mechanical watches, wind the spring".
watch plate falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Plates and bridges".
bridge falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Plates and bridges".
spring falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "clock or watch springs are, however, to be classified as clock or watch parts (heading 9114)".
hairspring falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Springs, including hairsprings".
mainspring falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "clock or watch springs are, however, to be classified as clock or watch parts (heading 9114)".
watch jewel falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "The term \"jewels\" includes substitutes for jewels".
watch part falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clock or watch parts".
clock part falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clock or watch parts".
watch plate is a kind of movement plate, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Plates and bridges".
bridge is a kind of movement plate, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Plates and bridges".
% the parts that note 1 names, so that note 1 can take them out
watch glass falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights".
watch crystal falls in the family watch part, as stated in the Wikipedia article Watch, confer "The crystal, also called the window or watch glass, is the transparent part of the case".
clock glass falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights".
clock weight falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights".
watch battery falls in the family watch part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Batteries entered with battery powered watches or clocks".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Note 1: what the chapter does not cover. Additional U.S. note 3: a
% battery entered alone.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
watch glass is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights (classified according to their constituent material)".
watch crystal is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights (classified according to their constituent material)".
clock glass is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights (classified according to their constituent material)".
clock weight is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock or watch glasses or weights (classified according to their constituent material)".
watch chain is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch chains (heading 7113 or 7117, as the case may be)".
bearing ball is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Bearing balls (heading 7326 or 8482, as the case may be)".
ball bearing is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Ball bearings (heading 8482)".
watch battery is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Batteries are otherwise classifiable in heading 8506 or 8507, whether or not suitable for use with watches or clocks".

% An article of the chapter: a good of one of its families, which note 1
% does not take out. A set or a composite good that names no kind of its
% own has the family of the component that gives it its essential
% character (gri.le).
rule note_91_1 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "This chapter does not cover":
a good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter ninety-one goods
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind that chapter ninety-one does not cover.

% Additional U.S. note 1(a): a watch is a timepiece for wearing or carrying
% on the person; a timepiece with a stand is no watch. A smart watch is no
% watch of heading 9102 (HQ H260060, below).
rule us_note_91_1a with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "The term \"watches\" embraces timepieces (including timepieces having special features, such as chronographs, calendar watches and watches designed for use in skin diving) of a kind for wearing or carrying on the person":
a good is a watch
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the family of the good is watch
    and it is not the case that
        the good incorporates a stand
    and it is not the case that
        the good differs substantially from the watches of heading 9102.

rule us_note_91_1a_stand with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Timepieces incorporating a stand, however simple, are not classifiable as watches":
a good is a clock
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the family of the good is watch
    and the good incorporates a stand.

rule clock_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks":
a good is a clock
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the family of the good is clock.

% A smart watch: a wearable electronic device in the form of a wrist watch
% whose principal design is to display, manipulate and store data. CBP
% finds that it differs substantially from the watches of heading 9102 and
% classifies it in heading 8517 (HQ H260060; also HQ H257947, HQ H273382).
% A quartz watch with an activity tracker stays a watch (HQ H271909): its
% kind is wrist watch, not smart watch.
rule smart_watch with provenance ruling HQ H260060,
        confer "Accordingly, CBP finds that the Apple Watch substantially differs from the articles described by heading 9102, HTSUS, and cannot be classified under the heading by application of GRI 1":
a good differs substantially from the watches of heading 9102
    if the kind of the good is smart watch.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The case of a watch (note 2). A case wholly of precious metal or of metal
% clad with precious metal, with or without pearls or stones; plating is no
% precious metal (Chapter 71 note 6). A case with a part of base metal (a
% steel back, a steel bezel) is not wholly of precious metal (HQ 968150,
% quoting the Explanatory Note), nor is a case of base metal inlaid with
% precious metal.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rule note_91_2_metal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Heading 9101 covers only watches with case wholly of precious metal or of metal clad with precious metal":
a watch has a case of precious metal
    if the case metal of the watch is a metal
    and the metal is a precious metal of the group a group
    and it is not the case that
        the case of the watch has a part of an other metal
        and the other metal is a base metal.

rule note_91_2_clad with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Heading 9101 covers only watches with case wholly of precious metal or of metal clad with precious metal":
a watch has a case of precious metal
    if the case of the watch is clad with a metal
    and the metal is a precious metal of the group a group
    and it is not the case that
        the case of the watch has a part of an other metal
        and the other metal is a base metal.

% a ruling that names only "a base metal" (NY N170879: "watch cases of base
% metal")
base metal is a base metal,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XV, confer "the expression \"base metals\" means".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Movements. Note 3: a watch movement does not exceed 12 mm in thickness
% and 50 mm in width, length or diameter; Additional U.S. note 1(d): a
% clock movement exceeds one of them.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rule note_91_3 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Such watch movements shall not exceed 12 mm in thickness and 50 mm in width, length or diameter":
a good is of watch size
    if the good measures a number mm in thickness
    and the number =< 12
    and the good measures an other number mm in width
    and the other number =< 50.

rule us_note_91_1d_thickness with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Such clock movements shall either exceed 12 mm in thickness or 50 mm in width, length or diameter, or both":
a good is of clock size
    if the good measures a number mm in thickness
    and the number > 12.

rule us_note_91_1d_width with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Such clock movements shall either exceed 12 mm in thickness or 50 mm in width, length or diameter, or both":
a good is of clock size
    if the good measures a number mm in width
    and the number > 50.

rule watch_movement_kind with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch movements, complete and assembled":
a good is a watch movement
    if the kind of the good is watch movement.

rule watch_movement_size with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "the expression \"watch movements\" means devices regulated by a balance wheel and hairspring, quartz crystal or any other system capable of determining intervals of time":
a good is a watch movement
    if the kind of the good is movement
    and the good is of watch size.

rule clock_movement_kind with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock movements, complete and assembled":
a good is a clock movement
    if the kind of the good is clock movement.

rule clock_movement_size with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "The term \"clock movements\" means devices regulated by a balance wheel and hairspring, quartz crystal or any other system capable of determining intervals of time":
a good is a clock movement
    if the kind of the good is movement
    and the good is of clock size.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% heading 9101: watches with a case of precious metal (note 2)
rule heading_9101 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches, with case of precious metal or of metal clad with precious metal":
a good is described by heading 9101
    if the good is a watch
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component has a case of precious metal.

% heading 9102: every other watch
rule heading_9102 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Wrist watches, pocket watches and other watches, including stop watches, other than those of heading 9101":
a good is described by heading 9102
    if the good is a watch
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component has a case of precious metal.

% heading 9103: clocks with watch movements; heading 9105: other clocks
rule heading_9103 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Clocks with watch movements, excluding clocks of heading 9104":
a good is described by heading 9103
    if the good is a clock
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component has a watch movement.

rule heading_9105 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks":
a good is described by heading 9105
    if the good is a clock
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and it is not the case that
        the component has a watch movement.

% headings 9108 and 9109: movements, complete and assembled
rule heading_9108 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch movements, complete and assembled":
a good is described by heading 9108
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is a watch movement.

rule heading_9109 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Clock movements, complete and assembled":
a good is described by heading 9109
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is a clock movement.

% headings 9104, 9106, 9107, 9110 to 9114: the family the heading names
rule heading_by_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "CLOCKS AND WATCHES AND PARTS THEREOF":
a good is described by heading a heading
    if the good is an article of chapter ninety-one
    and the family of the good is a family
    and the family is the family of heading the heading.

% Additional U.S. note 2: a strap, band or bracelet entered with a wrist
% watch, of a kind normally sold with it, is classified with the watch in
% heading 9101 or 9102 (the tariff gives it its own lines there, below six
% digits: NY N248589, 9102.12.40); otherwise it is of heading 9113 (NY
% N342931: a box set of a watch and an additional strap, 9102.11).
rule us_note_91_2 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets entered with wrist watches and of a kind normally sold therewith, whether or not attached, are classified with the watch in heading 9101 or 9102":
a good is described by heading a heading
    if the good is entered with a watch
    and the family of the good is watch strap
    and the heading is in [9101, 9102]
    and the watch is described by heading the heading.

rule us_note_91_2_otherwise with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Otherwise, watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets shall be classified in heading 9113":
a good is excluded from heading 9113
    if the good is entered with a watch
    and the watch is a watch.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Exclusions from other chapters.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Chapter 39 note 2(v): articles of Chapter 91 (clock or watch cases) are
% not of Chapter 39
rule note_39_2v with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles of chapter 91 (for example, clock or watch cases)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and the other heading is in [9101, 9102, 9103, 9104, 9105, 9106, 9107, 9108, 9109, 9110, 9111, 9112, 9113, 9114]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Chapter 71 note 3(l): clocks and watches are not of Chapter 71
rule note_71_3l with provenance HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71,
        confer "Articles of chapter 90, 91 or 92 (scientific instruments, clocks and watches, musical instruments)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 7101
    and the heading <= 7118
    and the other heading is in [9101, 9102, 9103, 9104, 9105, 9106, 9107, 9108, 9109, 9110, 9111, 9112, 9113, 9114]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% Chapter 42 note 4: watch straps are no clothing accessories of heading
% 4203
rule note_42_4 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "wrist straps, but excluding watch straps (heading 9113)":
a good is excluded from heading 4203
    if the good is described by heading 9113.

% GRI 3(a): heading 4205 ("Other articles of leather") is a general
% description; a watch case, a clock case, a watch strap or a watch part of
% leather is named by its own heading (HQ 951467: leather watch straps,
% 9113.90)
rule gri_3a_4205 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 4205
    if the heading is in [9111, 9112, 9113, 9114].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6: what the subheadings read.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule timepiece_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [9101, 9102, 9103, 9105, 9108, 9109]
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the timepiece form of the component is a form
    and the power class of the component is a power
    and the display class of the component is a display
    and the winding class of the component is a winding
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the form the form with power the power with display the display with winding the winding is the code under table timepieces.

% the subheading of a strap entered with a watch is the watch's
rule us_note_91_2_subheading with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "are classified with the watch in heading 9101 or 9102":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the good is entered with a watch
    and the heading is in [9101, 9102]
    and the subheading of the watch in heading the heading is the code.

rule timepiece_part_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [9104, 9106, 9107, 9110, 9111, 9112, 9113, 9114]
    and the part class of the good in heading the heading is a class
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the part class the class is the code under table timepiece parts.

% The form: of a watch, wrist watch or other (a pocket watch, a pendant
% watch); of a clock, its group; of a movement
rule form_wrist with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Wrist watches, electrically operated, whether or not incorporating a stop watch facility":
the timepiece form of a good is wrist
    if the good is a watch
    and the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of wrist watch.

rule form_other_watch with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: Electrically operated: 9101.91":
the timepiece form of a good is other watch
    if the good is a watch
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of wrist watch.

rule form_alarm with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Alarm clocks":
the timepiece form of a good is alarm
    if the good is a clock
    and the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of alarm clock.

rule form_wall with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Wall clocks":
the timepiece form of a good is wall
    if the good is a clock
    and the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of wall clock.

rule form_other_clock with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other clocks":
the timepiece form of a good is other clock
    if the good is a clock
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of alarm clock
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is an other kind
        and the other kind is a kind of wall clock.

rule form_movement with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch movements, complete and assembled":
the timepiece form of a good is movement
    if the family of the good is movement.

% The power: electrically operated (a battery powered quartz movement, NY
% N172320), or mechanical (driven by a spring)
rule power_electric with provenance ruling NY N172320,
        confer "which provides for other clocks: alarm clocks: electrically operated: other":
the power class of a good is electric
    if the good is electrically operated.

rule power_mechanical with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other wrist watches, whether or not incorporating a stop watch facility":
the power class of a good is mechanical
    if the good has a mechanical movement
    and it is not the case that
        the good is electrically operated.

% The display: mechanical (hands) or opto-electronic (digital), or both
rule display_mechanical with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "With mechanical display only":
the display class of a good is mechanical
    if the good has a mechanical display
    and it is not the case that
        the good has an opto-electronic display.

rule display_opto with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "With opto-electronic display only":
the display class of a good is opto-electronic
    if the good has an opto-electronic display
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a mechanical display.

rule display_combined with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: 9102.19":
the display class of a good is combined
    if the good has a mechanical display
    and the good has an opto-electronic display.

% a device of this model, with no provenance: a display the facts do not
% state, which only the rows that do not read the display accept
rule display_unstated:
the display class of a good is unstated
    if the family of the good is a family
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a mechanical display
    and it is not the case that
        the good has an opto-electronic display.

rule winding_automatic with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "With automatic winding":
the winding class of a good is automatic
    if the good has automatic winding.

rule winding_none with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: 9102.29":
the winding class of a good is none
    if the family of the good is a family
    and it is not the case that
        the good has automatic winding.

% The material of a case or a strap: what the good is classified as
% consisting of (GRI 3(b); HQ 951467: a leather strap with spring bars is
% classified by the strap). Precious metal or metal clad with precious
% metal beyond minor constituents (Chapter 71 notes 2(a), 4, 5, 7); base
% metal, whether or not plated; or another material, which the facts must
% name.
rule material_precious with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Of precious metal or of metal clad with precious metal":
the material class of a thing is precious
    if the thing is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component contains precious metal beyond minor constituents.

rule material_base_metal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Of base metal, whether or not gold- or silver-plated":
the material class of a thing is base metal
    if the thing is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is of base metal
    and it is not the case that
        the component contains precious metal beyond minor constituents.

rule material_other with provenance ruling HQ H276954,
        confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets may be of any material, for example, base metal, precious metal, leather, plastics or textile material":
the material class of a thing is other
    if the thing is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component is of a material other than metal
    and it is not the case that
        the component contains precious metal beyond minor constituents
    and it is not the case that
        the component is of base metal.

rule other_material_plastics with provenance ruling HQ H276954,
        confer "the Modal and Modal Sports bands of bovine leather and plastic, respectively, are classified in subheading 9113.90.80":
a thing is of a material other than metal
    if the thing is of plastics.

rule other_material_named with provenance ruling HQ H276954,
        confer "the Modal and Modal Sports bands of bovine leather and plastic, respectively, are classified in subheading 9113.90.80":
a thing is of a material other than metal
    if the thing is wholly or mainly of a material.

rule other_material_listing with provenance ruling HQ H276954,
        confer "the Modal and Modal Sports bands of bovine leather and plastic, respectively, are classified in subheading 9113.90.80":
a thing is of a material other than metal
    if the thing names only materials other than metal.

% Chapter 71 note 7: base metal inlaid with precious metal is metal clad
% with precious metal, except where the context requires otherwise (note 2
% to this chapter, for the case of a watch). A steel bracelet inlaid with
% gold is of 9113.10 (HQ 965207).
rule note_71_7_inlaid with provenance HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71,
        confer "Except where the context otherwise requires, the expression also covers base metal inlaid with precious metal":
a thing is of metal clad with precious metal
    if the thing is inlaid with a metal
    and the metal is a precious metal of the group a group.

% The class of a good in its heading
rule class_9104 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "vessels: 9104.00":
the part class of a good in heading 9104 is any
    if the family of the good is vehicle clock.

rule class_9106_recorder with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Time registers; time-recorders":
the part class of a good in heading 9106 is time recorder
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [time recorder, time register].

rule class_9106_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: 9106.90":
the part class of a good in heading 9106 is other
    if the family of the good is time apparatus
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is in [time recorder, time register].

rule class_9107 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "synchronous motor: 9107.00":
the part class of a good in heading 9107 is any
    if the family of the good is time switch.

% heading 9110: of watches (for a watch, or of the size of a watch
% movement), the three kinds of sets; otherwise "Other"
rule class_9110_watch with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Of watches":
the part class of a good in heading 9110 is a kind
    if the kind of the good is the kind
    and the good is for a watch
    and the kind is in [movement set, incomplete movement, rough movement].

rule class_9110_watch_size with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Of watches":
the part class of a good in heading 9110 is a kind
    if the kind of the good is the kind
    and the good is of watch size
    and it is not the case that
        the good is for a watch
    and the kind is in [movement set, incomplete movement, rough movement].

rule class_9110_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: 9110.90":
the part class of a good in heading 9110 is other
    if the family of the good is movement set
    and it is not the case that
        the good is for a watch
    and it is not the case that
        the good is of watch size.

% heading 9111: cases by their material; parts of cases
rule class_9111_case with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Watch cases and parts thereof":
the part class of a good in heading 9111 is a class
    if the kind of the good is watch case
    and the material class of the good is the class.

rule class_9111_part with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Parts: 9111.90":
the part class of a good in heading 9111 is part
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of case part.

rule class_9112_case with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Cases: 9112.20":
the part class of a good in heading 9112 is case
    if the kind of the good is clock case.

rule class_9112_part with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "9112.90.00":
the part class of a good in heading 9112 is part
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of case part.

% heading 9113: straps, bands and bracelets and their parts, by material
rule class_9113 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91,
        confer "Watch straps, watch bands and watch bracelets, and parts thereof":
the part class of a good in heading 9113 is a class
    if the material class of the good is the class.

% heading 9114: dials, plates and bridges, the other parts
rule class_9114_dial with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Dials: 9114.30":
the part class of a good in heading 9114 is dial
    if the kind of the good is dial.

rule class_9114_plate with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Plates and bridges: 9114.40":
the part class of a good in heading 9114 is plate
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of movement plate.

rule class_9114_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 91, confer "Other: 9114.90":
the part class of a good in heading 9114 is other
    if the family of the good is watch part
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is dial
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of movement plate.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests: goods with the facts a reader writes from a ruling or a listing.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% Watches: the case (note 2), the form, the power, the display, the winding
scenario watches is:
    % a quartz wrist watch with a case of 18 karat gold
    the kind of watch A is wrist watch.
    watch A is electrically operated.
    watch A has a mechanical display.
    the case metal of watch A is gold alloy.
    % a case of sterling silver with a steel bezel (HQ 968150) -> 9102
    the kind of watch B is wrist watch.
    watch B is electrically operated.
    watch B has a mechanical display.
    the case metal of watch B is silver alloy.
    the case of watch B has a part of stainless steel.
    % a gold-plated case with a stainless steel back (NY E83962) -> 9102.11
    the kind of watch C is wrist watch.
    watch C is electrically operated.
    watch C has a mechanical display.
    the case metal of watch C is brass.
    % an LED watch (NY N248589) -> 9102.12
    the kind of watch D is wrist watch.
    watch D is electrically operated.
    watch D has an opto-electronic display.
    % hands and a digital display
    the kind of watch E is wrist watch.
    watch E is electrically operated.
    watch E has a mechanical display.
    watch E has an opto-electronic display.
    % an automatic watch (NY N303322) -> 9102.21
    the kind of watch F is wrist watch.
    watch F has a mechanical movement.
    watch F has automatic winding.
    watch F has a mechanical display.
    % a hand-wound watch with a gold case
    the kind of watch G is wrist watch.
    watch G has a mechanical movement.
    watch G has a mechanical display.
    the case metal of watch G is gold alloy.
    % a quartz pendant watch (NY N233953) -> 9102.91
    the kind of watch H is pendant watch.
    watch H is electrically operated.
    watch H has a mechanical display.
    % a mechanical pocket watch with a case clad with gold
    the kind of watch I is pocket watch.
    watch I has a mechanical movement.
    the case of watch I is clad with gold.
    % a quartz watch whose display is not stated: the heading only
    the kind of watch J is wrist watch.
    watch J is electrically operated.
